{
  "schema": "sysid.acceptance/1",
  "written": "2026-11-05, before any identification code: the oracle's ruler (Zach, PROJECT - Sim2Real, Proposed Work Flow Nov 5 2026: 'if we assumed the simulator data was real, we should check that our system ID can match the real values')",
  "rule": "a parameter passes when |recovered - true| <= tol (abs) or <= tol x |true| (rel); every gated parameter's nominal value must FAIL its own tolerance, so a fit that returns the description unchanged fails; every hidden value is gated; a metric passes when before / after >= its factor on the held-out split. Tolerances are what the use needs (feed-forward, a pick on a moving belt, a 5 mm tool budget), not what a method happens to reach.",
  "examples": {
    "pendulum_can11": {
      "parameters": {
        "can11.gravity_nm": ["rel", 0.02],
        "can11.gravity_bottom_rad": ["abs", 0.005],
        "can11.armature_kg_m2": ["rel", 0.05],
        "can11.frictionloss_nm": ["rel", 0.1],
        "can11.friction_stribeck_drop_nm": ["rel", 0.25],
        "can11.friction_stribeck_speed_rad_s": ["rel", 0.3],
        "can11.damping_nm_s_rad": ["rel", 0.2],
        "can11.backlash_rad": ["rel", 0.1]
      },
      "metrics": {"held_out_link_fidelity": 4.0},
      "selected_rung": "M4"
    },
    "ur5e": {
